@startuml
title BeeGreen Backend API Architecture (SRS-driven)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

rectangle "Client Applications" as Clients {
  component "Website\n(React/TypeScript)" as WebClient
  component "Browser Extension\n(Chrome)" as ExtensionClient
}

node "Backend API Tier\n(Node.js + LoopBack)" as Backend {
  component "Users Controller" as UsersCtrl
  component "Ping Controller" as PingCtrl
  component "UserRepository" as UserRepo
}

interface "Users API\n/ users\n- POST create\n- GET list [filter]\n- PATCH bulk update [where]\n- GET /{id}" as UsersAPI
interface "Diagnostics API\n/ ping\n- GET ping" as PingAPI

database "Persistent Storage" as DB
component "Scoring & Recommendation\nData Processing" as Scoring <<external>>

WebClient --> UsersAPI : HTTP / JSON
WebClient --> PingAPI  : HTTP / JSON
ExtensionClient --> UsersAPI : HTTP / JSON
ExtensionClient --> PingAPI  : HTTP / JSON

UsersCtrl - UsersAPI
PingCtrl  - PingAPI

UsersCtrl --> UserRepo
UserRepo --> DB

Backend ..> Scoring : uses (out-of-scope details)

note right of UsersAPI
JSON bodies:
- Create: NewUser (id excluded)
- List: optional filter parameter
- Bulk update: partial User + optional where
- Read by id: path 'id' (string)
end note

note right of PingAPI
Response JSON:
- greeting (string)
- date (string)
- url (string)
- headers (object, additional properties allowed)
end note

note bottom of DB
Data entities:
User:
- id (string, generated)
- ip (string)
- creationDate (date)
- purchaseIds (string[])
- username (string)
- region (string)

InventoryItem:
- id (string, generated)
- stats (object)
- totalScore (number)
- category (string)
- details (string)
- comments (object[])
- name (string)
- associatedStores (string[])
end note

note top of Backend
Constraints:
- LoopBack REST + Repository abstractions
- Media type: application/json
- Ping depends on request context
end note

@enduml